# Review package: batch 6, slice cert

## a98a7fe0 Keep the link's certificate in the database and run the tunnel in https mode when it may

The https of a company's link is to end on the company's own machine. This adds what that needs to be kept and to be
acted on: the link_tls row (migration 0055_link_tls), with both private keys only as encryptSecret gives them and hidden
from the agents' database roles; ACME_DIRECTORY, which picks the CA or turns certificates off; and the tunnel's mode,
which tunnel.json carries and frpc follows. The file never holds a certificate or a key.

linkMode decides the mode from the database alone, so a restart writes the same tunnel settings at once. It says https
only for a certificate of the link's own name and host with more than 24 hours left and its own key. Anything else, a
throw too, means http, which still works through the relay's TLS, so ACME_DIRECTORY=off and a restart are the way back.
http mode's frpc config stays byte for byte what it was, and a tunnel.json from before this reads as http.

Proved by the plan's Done when, from apps/server: 136 tests pass in client, tunnel, link, orchestrator-control,
migrations, migration-metadata, compose and config, and tsc prints nothing. Each new test was seen to fail first; the
test of settings with no mode passed once Settings was exported, so it was seen to fail with the default taken out.

Ruling: link.test.ts's second tunnel.json equality, in the take-over test, also gains mode: 'http' - why: the plan names only the one at line 67, but `hornhoof link` writes through writeTunnelSettings as well - cost if wrong: none, one expected value in a test.
Ruling: tunnel.ts exports the Settings schema - why: the plan's test of settings with no mode has to read a file the way the keeper does, and the keeper's parse is private - cost if wrong: one more exported name, and plan 2 Task 6 touches this file anyway.
Ruling: updateTls throws 'The link has no certificate row to change.' when the row is missing - why: the plan says the row must exist, and a change that finds none would silently lose what the manager decided - cost if wrong: Task 8 meets a throw on a path it expected to do nothing, inside the pass that already logs and retries.
Ruling: store.ts also exports mayRunHttps, the pure part of linkMode, with its boundary test in link.test.ts - why: exactly 24 hours left needs a fixed clock, and linkMode's signature is the plan's - cost if wrong: one more exported name.
Ruling: tests beyond the plan's list, in the plan's files: a certificate of another host, no key, a key that is no key, a row in http mode, tests' default of off, a chain's first certificate, and the row's save and update - why: each is a branch of the plan's rule that nothing else would show - cost if wrong: a few more lines of test.

