## c9a67dd2 Split loadConfig and the grant texts where the certificate's change reached them, and count the new migration

The author check on the first commit was red for three reasons, each found before this fix. migration-history.test.ts
pins the number of migrations, so it now says 55, as Task 3's change said 54. loadConfig scores CRAP 23 whatever its
coverage, and adding acmeDirectory makes it a changed function, so it is split by what it reads. Adding link_tls to
HIDDEN brings agent-sql.ts under dryer, which finds grantsFor and readerGrantsFor to be one shape with one repeated line.

The structure changed and the behaviour did not: the config and health tests stay as they were and pass, and grantsFor
and readerGrantsFor give texts with the same SHA-256 before and after, checked by a script outside the repository.
Proved from apps/server: 138 tests pass in migration-history, client, tunnel, link, orchestrator-control, migrations,
migration-metadata, compose and config; tsc prints nothing; eslint on the changed files prints nothing; dryer finds no
pair in the changed files.

Ruling: loadConfig is split with the same functions as plan 2 Task 3's 3fbe15c9 (secretOf, nodeKeyOf, checkedEnv, buildOf, placesOf, limitsOf), word for word, and acmeDirectory sits apart from where that task adds keeper - why: both tasks hit the same gate on the same function, and one split lands more easily than two - cost if wrong: whoever lands the second resolves about one line in loadConfig's return.
Ruling: role in agent-sql.ts now takes the rights as a function and readVisible holds the repeated GRANT line - why: the file is one Task 7 must change, and dryer scored the old pair 1.00 - cost if wrong: plans 3 and 4, which change this file, meet a little more moved text; the SQL is the same.

